r full output can stop mining.
guide.nexustech.chapter.reator=Nuclear reactor
guide.nexustech.page.reator.0=The reactor is under development. Check the structure and GUI messages in the installed version; safety, heat and production rules may change.
guide.nexustech.page.reator.1=Build a solid 3x3 structure 5 blocks tall: 1 controller in the middle of the lower front row, facing outward; 1 core in the center of the third layer; fill the other 43 positions with nuclear casings.
guide.nexustech.page.reator.2=Open the formed controller. Use only nuclear fuel or a Nexus uranium ingot in the fuel slot. Put a water bucket in the middle slot and remove the empty bucket on the right; the tank holds up to 8,000 mB and accepts water pipes. Press On.
guide.nexustech.page.reator.3=Water helps cool the reactor and temperature does not drop below zero. After a safety shutdown (SCRAM), water speeds cooling above 400; wait until 400 or below and restart manually. Without water, the reactor can heat up.
guide.nexustech.chapter.mobs=Mobs and transport
guide.nexustech.page.mobs.0=Mob card: hold it in the offhand and directly kill an eligible mob. The first kill binds the type; only direct kills of that type count. Projectiles and machines do not count.
guide.nexustech.page.mobs.1=Examples: pig, cow, zombie and skeleton require 20 kills; enderman, blaze, witch and cave spider 10; ghast 5. A completed card can be used in the generator.
guide.nexustech.page.mobs.2=Mob generator: insert a completed card and supply FE; check space and nearby mob limits. Defaults are configurable on the server. Only certain vanilla mobs are accepted.
guide.nexustech.page.mobs.3=Fan: place facing the corridor, supply FE and set speed and range in the GUI. It pushes items and living entities; walls, blocks and unloaded chunks can block airflow.
guide.nexustech.page.mobs.4=Conveyor moves items and living entities in its direction. Spike crusher damages targets using FE; cards adjust damage, loot, fire or efficiency. Player protection is on by default.
guide.nexustech.page.mobs.5=Fire cards add fire damage but do not guarantee ignition or cooked drops. Looting depends on loot tables and does not count as a player kill.
guide.nexustech.chapter.equipamento=Equipment and parts
guide.nexustech.page.equipamento.0=Tech tools: hold the tool in your main hand and press G to adjust speed and area. On mobile, map the key. Area mining obeys restrictions and permissions.
guide.nexustech.page.equipamento.1=Tech armor: equip pieces normally. The helmet offers night vision; flight is not implemented. Other night-vision effects may interfere.
guide.nexustech.page.equipamento.2=Tech circuit boards, coils, gears, frames, conductors, contacts, meshes, casings, panels and rotors are crafting components. Search their names in the catalog.
guide.nexustech.chapter.ponte=Storage bridge
guide.nexustech.page.ponte.0=The ProjectE–SSN bridge is experimental and diagnostic: it shows adjacency information, but does not transfer items or EMC or functionally connect the networks.

